(a) whether Government has conducted any study regarding air pollution and environmental impact in urban and industrial areas located near thermal power plants;
(b) whether cumulative environmental impact assessments have been conducted for clusters where thermal power plants operate along with other polluting industries such as refineries, chemical units and diesel-based facilities;
(c) whether Government proposes stricter emission norms, continuous monitoring systems and public disclosure of emission data particularly for older units; and
(d) whether any measures are proposed for environmental mitigation and health protection in highly polluted industrial clusters?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding accessibility of advanced Cancer treatment facilities in Andhra Pradesh;
(b) whether Government has assessed the requirement for additional regional Cancer treatment and research centres in North Coastal Andhra Pradesh and Rayalaseema;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of projects sanctioned under Swadesh Darshan 2.0 and PRASHAD schemes in Andhra Pradesh during 2024-25 and 2025-26, along with the amounts sanctioned and released thereunder;
(b) whether any proposals from the State under the said schemes are pending approval; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of delay in implementation of the Integrated Aqua Park approved in Bapatla district of Andhra Pradesh on employment generation and aqua exports;
(b) the timelines fixed for completion of the project and the present status thereof;
(c) whether Government has received any proposal from Government of Andhra Pradesh for revision of project cost or additional Central assistance for the project;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment regarding the integration of AYUSH systems with preventive healthcare and management of non-communicable diseases, particularly in States such as Andhra Pradesh where lifestyle diseases are rising;
(b) if so, the details thereof including institutions, funding support and programmes approved for Andhra Pradesh; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding adequacy of Apna Ghar facilities along major freight and industrial corridors in the State of Andhra Pradesh;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has identified National Highways and logistics corridors in the State of Andhra Pradesh requiring additional Apna Ghar facilities for truck drivers;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the CSMC recently approved 3.52 lakh houses under PMAY-Urban 2.0 and if so, the number of houses, cities covered and Central funds committed specifically for Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the total Central funds released to Andhra Pradesh under PMAY-U Phases I and II, the number of houses completed and the number of these completed houses currently lying vacant; and
(c) whether the Ministry has received representations to include Amaravati land-pooling farmers as eligible beneficiaries under PMAY-U 2.0 or a special housing category and the details of the action taken thereon?

(a) whether Government has a mechanism in place to ensure timely and regular audits of Multi State Co-operative Societies (MSCSs) in the country;
(b) if so, the details of audits conducted in the last three years, including the number of MSCSs audited; and
(c) whether any irregularity was found in these audits, and if so, the steps taken by Government to address them?

(a) the total tribal population in Andhra Pradesh, district-wise;
(b) the funds allocated and utilized for tribal welfare schemes;
(c) the number of Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRSs) established in the State;
(d) whether any proposals are pending for inclusion of tribal communities; and
(e) the steps taken to improve livelihood opportunities?

(a) whether Government is aware that Nandaluru Railway Station, located on the Mumbai–Chennai route in the Renigunta–Kadapa Section, earlier functioned as an interchanging junction with a Loco Shed and watering point due to availability of quality surface water from the Cheyyeru River;
(b) whether it  is a fact that 170 acres of vacant Railway land is available at Nandaluru; and
(c) whether Government proposes to revive railway operations there, particularly in view of Guntakal and Renigunta divisions presently depending on borewell water?

(a) whether Government has received and considered Andhra Pradesh’s request to increase Central subsidy support for micro-irrigation from 55 per cent to 90 per cent for small and marginal farmers in Andhra Pradesh, especially in drought prone districts of Rayalaseema region;
(b) if so, the status of approval, amount of Central funds committed and timeline for rollout;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) the criteria under the Central Micro-Irrigation Fund/subsidy scheme for subsidy rate increases and the manner in which it aligns with Andhra Pradesh's request; and 
(e) the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of monument conservation projects approved and completed in Andhra Pradesh since 2021;
(b) the funds sanctioned, released and utilised by the Archaeological Survey of India for conservation works in the State during this period;
(c) whether any proposals have been received for private sector participation in monument conservation under the National Culture Fund or similar models and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure time-bound approvals, effective monitoring and accountability in conservation projects in Andhra Pradesh?

(a) whether any work has started on the development of spectrum options, which is basic infrastructure of 6G technology;
(b) whether any study has been conducted to unearth the business applications and key technologies of 6G technology;
(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether any specific budget has been allocated for the development of 6G technology; and
(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the total length of Expressways built under the PM-Gati Shakti in the country, State-wise;
(b) the current implementation status of expressways under the scheme in Andhra Pradesh; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to expedite the projects under the PM- Gati Shakti scheme in Andhra Pradesh?

(a) whether the Central Government is aware of complaints by fishermen on the Andhra coast (e.g. Kakinada/Uppada) regarding fish stock decline and alleged industrial pollution;
(b) if so, what investigations the Centre has initiated and whether the Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) has been requested to test sea-water and effluents;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether central support or compensation is available to affected fisher communities and criteria for eligibility; and
(e) if so, the details thereof including any central funds released, if not, reasons therefor?

(a) whether the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) central dashboard shows any blocks/mandals in the State of Andhra Pradesh where household tap-connection targets remain unachieved as on date and the reasons for gaps (forest permissions/land acquisition/quality);
(b) if so, the number of households still without functional taps and the Central funds released to Andhra Pradesh for JJM projects during the last two years;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) the central technical assistance (water quality labs, Fluoride mitigation technologies) that has been offered specifically for the State of Andhra Pradesh is high-Fluoride habitations;
(e) if so, the details thereof; and
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the steps taken to enhance the safety, efficiency and sustainability of existing and planned nuclear power plants, including investments in technology, infrastructure and workforce development;
(b) whether there are challenges or constraints in scaling up nuclear energy in India and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether the measures are being undertaken to address these challenges and, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the current status of India’s installed nuclear power capacity and the projected increase to 22, 480 MW by 2031-32, including the details on timeline and phases of development;
(b) the measures taken to enhance operational efficiency and safety of existing nuclear reactors, particularly the 24 reactors currently installed and the details regarding the 21 new reactors with a total capacity of 15,300 MW that are under various stages of implementation; and
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessments regarding the environmental impacts of expanding nuclear power capacity and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the present status of the cashless golden-hour treatment scheme for road accident victims, including its scope and operational framework and the details thereof;
(b) the States and Union Territories covered under the pilot phase so far and the outcomes achieved in terms of lives saved and claims settled;
(c) whether Andhra Pradesh has been included or proposed to be included under the scheme;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the timeline envisaged by Government for nationwide rollout of the cashless golden-hour treatment scheme?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of the Sagar Mitra programme in  Andhra Pradesh, particularly in coastal districts such as Kakinada, Nellore and Visakhapatnam;
(b) if so, the findings of the review and steps taken to improve outreach and awareness among fishers regarding Potential Fishing Zone (PFZ) advisories and Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) benefits;
(c) the district-wise number of Sagar Mitras currently deployed in the State; and
(d) whether any proposal has been received from the State Government for expanding the scheme to inland fisheries or upgrading the NABHIMITRA app, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the extent of urea supply shortfalls reported during the current fertilizer season, State-wise including the State of Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the allocation made by the Centre, stock position and distribution status of urea in Andhra Pradesh during the last six months;
(c) whether complaints or representations have been received from State authorities or farmer organisations regarding shortages, rationing or price-related issues and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by the Central Government to ensure timely availability of urea and other fertilizers in the State?

(a) whether the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) has completed its inquiry into the large-scale flight disruptions faced by IndiGo;
(b) whether any directions or corrective measures have been issued to airlines to ensure strict compliance with safety norms, crew duty and rest regulations;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) actions taken to ensure passenger refunds and compensation; and
(e) steps adopted to strengthen air traffic resilience during peak periods?

(a) the objectives and expected outcomes of India’s first analog space mission launched in Leh, including the specific challenges it aims to address for future lunar missions;
(b) the role of various organizations, including ISRO, AAKA Space Studio and academic institutions, in planning and execution of this mission and whether similar collaborations are planned for future space missions; and
(c) whether Government has identified any specific technologies or research initiatives stemming from this mission that could enhance India's capabilities in human spaceflight and exploration and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether India is presently reliant on China when it comes to accessing rare earth minerals;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has taken steps to develop its own rare earth mineral value chain;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is aware of the sharp decline in lemon yields in Andhra Pradesh due to extreme heat, especially in Rayalaseema region, despite strong demand and prices;
(b) whether measures are being taken to support affected farmers;
(c) whether steps are being considered to stabilize supply chains and ensure fair returns; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government proposes to formulate a comprehensive policy on the export and import of agricultural commodities to ensure stability and predictability for farmers and traders;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government plans to introduce a compensatory mechanism for farmers adversely impacted by sudden export bans, particularly in the case of onions, rice and other essential crops;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) whether Government intends to establish mechanisms to link farmers to global markets to enhance their income; and
(f) if so, the steps taken in this regard?

(a) the measures taken for the promotion and propagation of Classical Languages (Tamil, Sanskrit, Kannada, Telugu, Malayalam, and Odia);
(b) the details of language-wise level of grants and expenditures on each of the six languages;
(c) the number of the professional chairs of Classical Languages set up across various central Universities;
(d) whether Government intends on taking special measures for the promotion of Telugu language and literature; and
(e) whether Government plans to accord Classical status to the Pali language in light of its ancient origins and literary heritage?

(a) whether the provisions of the Bills of Lading Act, 2025 will be operationalised at all major and minor ports in the State of Andhra Pradesh;
(b) if so, whether training or capacity-building modules are planned for port officials and exporters; and
(c) the expected impact on trade logistics in Visakhapatnam and Kakinada ports?

(a) whether Government has launched initiatives to engage public in Parliamentary processes through education or outreach programmes;
(b) if so, the details of these programmes and their target audience; and
(c) whether Government plans to introduce new initiatives to increase public participation and awareness of legislative processes, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether there has been a reduction in domestic gas supplies by up to 20 per cent, thereby affecting the price of Compressed Natural Gas (CNG);
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the extent of the price increase per kg of CNG;
(c) whether any measures, such as a reduction in excise duty, are being considered to mitigate this impact; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, including the timeline for implementing such measures, particularly in key CNG markets like Mumbai and Delhi?

(a) the details of mechanised cleaning operational at railway stations in the country;
(b) whether the same has been restricted to areas of conducive surfaces furnished with tiles/kota stones;
(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the details of proposed measures to be taken in this respect to ensure better cleanliness at railway stations?

